<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Hasan ibn Kannun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 985</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as al-Hasan ibn Qannun, Al-Hasan ibn Qannun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Hasan ibn Kannun was the last Idrisid ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, holding territory in the north of the country in the mid-10th century between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> and the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. He surrendered to the Cordoban general Ghalib in 974 and was taken to Córdoba and then exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. Returning with Fatimid support in 985, he was defeated and executed.</p></div>
